File Index

/authTokenStore.ts
Purpose: Phase D — localStorage wrapper for the cloud-account bearer token (getToken/setToken/clearToken/isExpired), single key `shatteredArchive.auth.token`, matching this codebase's existing per-feature idiom (own STORAGE_KEY, inline try/catch, no shared wrapper — see useConnectModal.ts for the same shape). Also subscribeToToken() (2026-07-31): a `storage`-event subscription that is how the app window learns the login POPUP signed in — that event fires only in OTHER same-origin windows, never the writing one, which is exactly the popup→app direction. Unit-tested (authTokenStore.test.ts), including that jsdom needs the event dispatched manually.

/siteApi.ts
Purpose: Phase D — the C# service (Server.Web.Public) game-client pairs with. SITE_ORIGIN (absolute, for the login-start page navigation — not subject to CORS) vs. siteApiBase() (relative `/api/site` via the dev proxy in dev, avoiding CORS entirely; the real absolute origin in prod, relying on the Cors:AllowedOrigins tightening added alongside these endpoints). SITE_ORIGIN honours the VITE_SITE_API build arg in BOTH modes (2026-07-31) — the local container stack mirrors production but reaches the C# service at localhost:5000 — falling back with `||` not `??`, since an undeclared Docker ARG yields an empty string and the checked-in apps/game-client/.env would otherwise supply a dev value to every image.

/gameSso.ts
Purpose: Phase D — startLogin() runs this site's user/game-sso/start hand-off in a POPUP and resolves a LoginOutcome (success/cancelled/timeout/blocked); it never navigates this window, because doing so tore down the app and dropped the live telnet socket mid-session (2026-07-31). The popup returns to /auth-callback.html, whose localStorage write reaches here as a `storage` event (authTokenStore.subscribeToToken), with an interval as backstop that also catches the user dismissing the window; 3-minute ceiling, inside the C# side's 10-minute state cookie. The returnUrl path change needs no backend change — IsAllowedReturnOrigin validates ORIGIN only (UserController.cs:254). game-client still has no service key of its own — the C# backend performs the actual code exchange (key-custody constraint). Re-exports authFragment.ts's parseAuthFragment for convenience.

/authFragment.ts
Purpose: Phase D — the PURE parser for the game-sso callback's URL fragment (#auth_token=...&expires_at=... on success, #auth_error=1 on failure), deliberately split out of gameSso.ts: this repo's Jest "client" project cannot compile `import.meta` (which siteApi.ts uses) anywhere in a module's import graph, so the one genuinely testable piece lives with zero such imports. Unit-tested (authFragment.test.ts).

/cloudSync.ts
Purpose: Phase D — whole-collection fetch wrappers (loadScripts/saveScripts/loadPluginConfigs/savePluginConfigs/loadGlobalScripts/saveGlobalScripts) against the C# site's per-account UserContentController (api/user-content/scripts, api/user-content/plugin-configs, api/user-content/global-scripts). Global scripts sync as an ARRAY OF BUCKETS, one per connection, because this client keeps a separate global set per connection while the mobile client keeps one and owns only the "default" bucket. A 401 clears the stored token and reports `unauthenticated` rather than throwing, so callers can show a clean "please log in again" instead of crashing. Same `import.meta` (siteApi.ts) testability gap as gameSso.ts — verified live instead (see AccountModal/useAccountModal, plan doc Step 3 evidence).
